  "brief": "BILL is being acquired by TPG and Corpay in a $6 billion all-cash deal.\n\nTPG / BILL (Announced): BILL to Go Private. BILL is being acquired by TPG and Corpay in a $6 billion all-cash deal [1, 2, 3]. BILL will go private in a $6 billion deal led by TPG with Corpay [7]. BILL has agreed to be acquired by TPG in a partnership with Corpay [8]. TPG and Corpay will take BILL private in a $6 billion deal [5, 6, 4].\nBending Spoons / Mailchimp (Announced): Bending Spoons and Mailchimp Deal. Bending Spoons is buying Mailchimp from Intuit [9, 10, 11]. The deal is worth 3.32-3.68 billion Euros [9, 10]. Bending Spoons will announce a €1.18 billion private placement [11]. The acquisition has been announced [13].\nBeeline Holdings / TYTL (Announced): Beeline Holdings to Acquire TYTL. Beeline Holdings is acquiring TYTL in an all-stock deal [15, 16, 18]. The deal aims to expand into tokenized real estate and blockchain-enabled home equity finance [17, 18]. No further details on the deal have been announced [15, 16, 17].\nKKR / EdgeCore (Rumored): KKR to Buy EdgeCore. KKR is in talks to buy a majority stake in EdgeCore [19, 20]. The deal is valued at at least $8 billion [20]. No further information is available at this stage [19].\nSanofi / Insmed (Rumored): Sanofi to Takeover Insmed. Sanofi is considering a takeover of US drugmaker Insmed [21, 22]. The deal is still in its early stages [21, 22].\nWynnchurch Capital / Luxfer Holdings (Completed): Wynnchurch Capital Acquires Luxfer Holdings. Wynnchurch Capital has acquired Luxfer Holdings in a take-private deal [23, 24, 25]. The deal is now completed [23, 24].\nPalo Alto Networks / Applied Compute (Announced): Palo Alto Networks to Acquire Applied Compute. Palo Alto Networks is acquiring Applied Compute for $4.5 billion [26, 27, 28]. The deal was announced on November 18 and is expected to bring secure open-weight AI to the enterprise [29, 30]. No further information is available as the deal is still in the announced stage [26, 27, 28].\nAMPERA / Berto (Announced): AMPERA and Berto to Merge. AMPERA and Berto will combine in a multimillion-dollar deal [31]. The deal was announced on November 20 [31].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- NextEra-Dominion merger cleared by DoJ antitrust division [32].\n- HSBC Upgrades Tesla to 'Hold' — SpaceX Merger Math Explains Why [33].\n- Service Industries subsidiary explores clothing-chain acquisition [34].",
